<header><p class="st-kicker">margraviate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Brandenburg-Bayreuth</h1><p class="st-meta">1398 CE – 1791 CE · capital Bayreuth</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Franconian margraviate of the Hohenzollerns, ruled from Kulmbach and Bayreuth and made a rococo showcase by Margravine Wilhelmine.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollern</a> rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/burgraviate-of-nuremberg">Burgraviate of Nuremberg</a> divided their Franconian lands in 1398, the territory 'above the mountains' around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulmbach">Kulmbach</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plassenburg">Plassenburg</a> went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-iii-burgrave-of-nuremberg">John III</a>. After the family gained the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-brandenburg">Margraviate of Brandenburg</a> in 1415, its Franconian principalities were usually ruled by younger sons with the title of margrave.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-alcibiades-margrave-of-brandenburg-kulmbach">Albert Alcibiades</a> devastated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> in his wars of the 1550s. The territory was Lutheran, and the court moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulmbach">Kulmbach</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a> in the early 17th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelmine-of-bayreuth">Margravine Wilhelmine</a>, sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a>, and her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-margrave-of-brandenburg-bayreuth">Frederick</a> made Bayreuth a cultural centre, building the Margravial Opera House and founding the university at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erlangen">Erlangen</a> in 1743.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1769 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a> passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-alexander-margrave-of-brandenburg-ansbach">Charles Alexander</a>, margrave of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-brandenburg-ansbach">Principality of Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, who in 1791 ceded both principalities to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> gave Bayreuth to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria">Kingdom of Bavaria</a> in 1810. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-wagner">Richard Wagner</a> later built his festival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> in the town.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-brandenburg-bayreuth.jpg" alt="Principality of Brandenburg-Bayreuth" width="320" height="373"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wappen_Brandenburg_Ansbach_Kulmbach_Bayreuth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1398 CE – 1791 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>margraviate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bayreuth</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Albert Alcibiades, Frederick</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>East Franconian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Margraviate of Bayreuth, Brandenburg-Kulmbach</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1594&amp;focus=principality-of-brandenburg-bayreuth" aria-label="Principality of Brandenburg-Bayreuth on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4945 440 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Brandenburg-Bayreuth lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5265 696L5250 710M5265 696L5229 694M5265 696L5300 622